1086:| basis | a basis is a source-of-truth position (POSITION coordinates (stream, epoch, offset, ordinal)) plus a valid time |
1087:| eligibility | index I is eligible to serve basis B only when all hold: its watermark (a fully resolved prefix) has reached B in B's epoch; C1's eligibility for the query (mapping, valid time, exact cut); I can actually reconstruct B (a current-only index only when B is at or after the last change to every attribute the read touches, the validity interval of R18); and I has applied every erasure published so far, independently of B (ERASURE frontier) (RULINGS Q31d) |
1088:| watermarkRouting | a read that finds no eligible index waits at most T-WATERMARK-WAIT-MS for one, then routes to an eligible fallback (the source of truth's own query surface or another index); the fallback's latency counts in the read's own latency; the receipt records the route and the surface language, a cross-language fallback is counted per surface, and fallbacks are reported as a share of reads per window; no index answers for a basis it is not eligible for (RULINGS Q31d) |
1089:| ackOwnership | the source of truth sends the ACK after its own publication; read-your-own-write holds by routing (the pull at the returned position goes to an eligible index, else the fallback); in normal operation the current index is kept synchronous so the fast path serves that pull; during a current-index outage commits and ACKs continue, pulls fall back, the index catches up from the feed through a bounded queue, and fallback share and recovery time are measured (GS.04b); history and analytics stay asynchronous behind watermarks (RULINGS Q31e, replacing Q28's ACK clause) |
