  1172	| Item | Rule |
  1173	| --- | --- |
  1174	| coordinates | (stream, epoch, offset, ordinal): the source of truth's log stream and epoch, the engine's log offset (or the QLever broker's log frame) and the ordinal of a Triplex transact inside that engine transaction |
  1175	| order | lexicographic over (stream, epoch, offset, ordinal); positions need not be dense |
  1176	| nested | one engine transaction holding several Triplex transacts gives them consecutive ordinals at one offset, assigned atomically with the assertions and the subject compare-and-set |
  1177	| watermark | a fully resolved prefix: every position at or below it is applied or known aborted (stronger than the greatest position seen) |
  1178	| aborted | aborted offsets are accounted: the feed's resolution stream lists each one |
  1179	| epochs | a watermark from one epoch never satisfies a basis in another epoch without the mapping C1 defines |
  1180	| oracle | O-REPLAY treats positions as totally ordered coordinates: it sorts by coordinate and assigns its own dense ordinals for cuts |
  1181	| falsifiers | FX-NESTED-CUTS, FX-ABORT-GAP, FX-CRASH-APPEND-RESOLUTION, FX-RESUME-AT-ABORT-GAP |
