   443	## 5. Evidence model and closure
   444	
   445	### 5.1 Receipt schema
   446	
   447	| Field | Type |
   448	| --- | --- |
   449	| receiptId | string, unique |
   450	| runKind | acceptance \| calibration \| mutation \| verifier \| diagnostic |
   451	| contract | {version, transitiveSha256} |
   452	| obligations | [{id, definitionSha256}] |
   453	| lane | lane id for lane-scope receipts; for engine-scope receipts the scope key (layer, engine, imageDigest, configSha256, slot) derived from the composition assignment of the obligation's layer (COMPOSITION scopeKey) |
   454	| composition | {source, current, history, analytics}: each {engine: xtdb \| qlever, imageDigest, configSha256, slot} (RULINGS Q28); positionsDense: bool with its evidence (RULINGS Q32e; missing means non-dense) |
   455	| replicationEdges | [{from, to, consumerSourceSha256, translationGeneration}] for every edge of the composition |
   456	| watermarks | per read: {readId, basisPosition, servingIndex, watermarkAtRead, waitMs, route} |
   457	| trace | {generatorSourceSha256, seed, backgroundCommands, overlayCommands} (TARGETS 2.1 freeze; background and scenario overlay accounted separately) |
   458	| cpuQuota | {engineCores, hostBrokerCpu, kernelCpu} (TARGETS 1.1 P4 item 3) |
   459	| profileIdentity | {sourceTreeSha256 (including uncommitted and untracked executed inputs), buildManifestSha256, importedDist [{path, sha256}], lockfileSha256, node, pnpm, composition (per-assignment image digests, configuration hashes and slots), resourceCaps, enabledCapabilities [], fixtureSha256, gateScriptSha256, oracleFiles [{id, sha256}], caseManifests [{set, sha256}], projectionSpecVersion, logFormatVersion} |
   460	| endpoint | {contacted, expected} |
   461	| admission | {reservationId, forecast, observedPeaks} |
   462	| coRunners | [container ids] |
   463	| timing | {start, end} |
   464	| counts | {declared, executed, skipped, unsupported, notImplemented, unexpectedErrors} |
   465	| evidence | [evidence objects, each with kind and objectSha256 of its retained bytes under runs/objects] |
   466	| firstFailures | [evidence refs] |
   732	- **Inputs.** The captured command intent (ordered submissions with operations, typed values in canonical encoding, entity ids and types, valid intervals, preconditions, meta, enforcement mode and rules, nested-transaction structure), schema releases, and durable-decision evidence (engine commit evidence or the log of record read back, and the fault witness). ACK receipts bind only generated identities: assertion ids, txIds and recorded instants.
   733	- **Clocks.** Recorded instants are not assumed monotonic in position order; separate runtimes supply their own clocks (PLAN C1). Histories with equal and with decreasing recorded instants are first-class cases (EV-SAME-R, EV-DECREASING-R, CS-TEMPORAL decreasing-clock).
   734	- **R independent of P.** A cut is (scope, P, optional R, V). Recorded visibility is `recordedPosition <= P` and, when R is bound, `recordedAt <= R`, evaluated independently: an assertion with a later position but an earlier instant is invisible at P below its position, and an assertion at a lower position with an instant above R is invisible at R.
   735	- **Position accounting.** Positions are totally ordered coordinates (POSITION: (stream, epoch, offset, ordinal), lexicographic, not necessarily dense; RULINGS Q31c): the oracle sorts committed transacts by coordinate and assigns its own dense ordinals for cuts; nested transacts inside one engine transaction share one offset and take consecutive ordinals in callback order; aborted offsets are accounted from the feed's resolution stream; the oracle checks every receipt coordinate against the committed order and fails the run on a mismatch.
   736	- **Outcomes.** The oracle derives each command's expected outcome from intent, order, preconditions, enforcement (CN-NEW-OR-WORSENED) and durable-decision evidence (COMMIT_OUTCOMES), then compares the receipts' outcomes afterwards. A receipt never decides which command is valid or committed.
   737	- **Outputs.** Complete assertion metadata; raw-lifetime and as-of snapshot history; entity models (card-one value or E-CONFLICTING-VALUES per C5; card-many per CARD_MANY_ORDER; absent optional as a missing property; includes at the same basis; timelines); transaction records with ordered changes and the logical journal facts (C6); cursor page sequences; support counts; C1 eligibility routes (for O-PLAN); arithmetic, comparison and aggregate results per section 4; analytic scale counts per population stratum (SCALE_POPULATION, section S).
   738	- **Independence.** Python stdlib only; imports no repository code; its own exact integers and decimals, IEEE binary64 (via struct) and codepoint ordering; no casefolding.
   739	- **Self-checks before ACCEPTED.** Reproduce O-HAM finite-nine, O-CFG8 tiny-v4 and the O-EVT cut semantics where domains overlap; unit tests for every table row of section 4.
   740	
   741	### 6.2 O-SHAPE
   742	
   743	Each case file entry carries: resultSemantics: set | bag | ordered; groupingKey: list of variables with COMPARISON_RULES identity; unboundHandling: exclude-row | null-cell (stated per projected variable); comparator: CMP-SET-ROWS | CMP-BAG-ROWS | CMP-ORDERED-ROWS; expectedRows; citation (SPARQL 1.1 or SQL section, or the packet task).
   744	
   745	- Packet-derived shapes use set semantics (runner sorted-unique comparison).
   746	- Negation controls compare the projected entity set.
   747	- Aggregate controls follow AGGREGATE_RULES; empty groups per AG-EMPTY-*.
   748	- Tied extremes keep every witness row (AG-MINMAX-TIES).
   749	- An unbound projected variable is a null cell only where the case says null-cell; otherwise the row is excluded.
   750	
   751	### 6.3 O-OBS protocols
   752	
   753	| Protocol | Evidence fields | Verdict |
   754	| --- | --- | --- |
   755	| OBS-CANCEL | requestId, connectionId, tCancelRequested, tCallerSettled, callerError, transportAck {kind, t}, engineActiveSamples [{t, activeQueryIds}], tDrained, reuseQueryId, tReuseOk | PASS iff callerError matches E-CANCELLED or E-TIMEOUT as the case pins, transportAck observed, the request id absent from every engine sample after tDrained with tDrained - tCancelRequested <= T-DRAIN-MS, sample gaps <= 1000 ms over [tCancelRequested, tDrained + 5000 ms], and the reuse query on the same connection succeeds |
   756	| OBS-PREABORT | requestId, engineStatementLog [{t, tag}], coverage | PASS iff zero engine statements carry the request id over the full coverage window |
   757	| OBS-CONNECTIONS | poolDeclarations [{label, max}], engineConnectionSamples [{t, label, count}], baseline, tClose | PASS iff every sample <= declared max and the count equals baseline within T-CONN-RELEASE-MS after tClose |
   758	| OBS-SCRATCH | relation, countBefore, countAfter, resolutionReceipts | PASS iff countAfter = countBefore for every scratch relation and every unknown working outcome is resolved |
