   193	## 5. Correct but not tuned (from the paste)
   194	
   195	Global serializability is not needed. Everything in the ten goals must still be correct; only P1 to P5 and the secondary
   196	measurements are tuned. Performance bars that do not map to a priority workload (for example a general recursion latency bar, latency
   197	growth from 1m to 10m for arbitrary selective queries, deep-page cost) are reported secondary measurements with no authority to block
   253	4. Plan-impact preview (GS.11) and activation (GS.10) are compared at one common input basis, never at different bases.
   254	5. Every scenario carries positive witnesses (subjects that must change) and negative witnesses (subjects that must not).
   255	6. **Workload coverage is frozen before any comparison and reviewed independently (Codex round 2, finding 18),** so a sweep of mostly
   256	   no-op evaluations cannot pass P5. Provisional floors: R2 changes the outputs of at least 20% of in-scope subjects; every rule fires
   257	   for at least 5% of subjects; work-location fanout follows a seeded Zipf (s = 1.0) over 2,000 locations at the 100k rung, so the
   258	   largest location holds hundreds of workers; at least 1% of evaluations each produce three or more work items.
   259	7. **Domain-dependent comparisons are blocked** until W0's SPEC.md, releases and golden cases have passed an independent review
   260	   (V-D01) and their hashes are pinned in the contract.
