2345:- Statement: Under TARGETS 1.1 P3: feed entries carry tx, entity, attribute and the valid-time range affected; commit time is the source's publication instant on the shared host monotonic clock; the cursor is (epoch, position); the expected affected-subject set per transaction is the directly written subjects (O-REPLAY) plus subjects affected through referenced entities under WORLD_W0 (O-DOMAIN, NS-P3-DOMAIN-AFFECTED-SET); 'affected subjects known' is the consumer's single durable write of the set and its checkpoint. Over a run there are zero gaps (NS-P3-GAPS-MAX) and zero per-subject order violations (NS-P3-ORDER-VIOLATIONS-MAX); lag stays within NS-P3-LAG-P99-MS with P1's 256 readers running; delivery is at-least-once from the last checkpoint with effects keyed by (consumer, position, subject), so crashes before the effect, after the effect before the checkpoint, and after the checkpoint (NS-P3-CRASH-BEFORE-EFFECT, NS-P3-CRASH-AFTER-EFFECT, NS-P3-CRASH-AFTER-CHECKPOINT) leave zero visible duplicate effects (NS-P3-VISIBLE-DUP-EFFECTS-MAX) while replay attempts are counted separately; resume from a checkpoint replays exactly.
