1748:**`G7.journal.logical-contract`: The logical journal stays queryable (C6).**
1749:- Statement: Every C6-* case: direct match and Datalog queries over :_tx/change and :_tx/changed-entity, transactions(), transactionsForEntity and transactionByCommand return O-REPLAY's outputs per JOURNAL_RULES: creation order (JN-ORDER), staged facts visible to later operations of the same command (JN-STAGED), bit-exact -0.0 change values (JN-NEGZERO, RULINGS Q21 AMB-04, provisional, flagged for Sam) and the documented and testkit-pinned fields (JN-FIELDS); whole-journal byte identity of a physically slimmed journal is checked against a separate T0-capture baseline (C6-SLIM-BYTE-IDENTICAL), modulo erasure: both sides replace erased values with their markers first (ER-JOURNAL-MODULO, RULINGS Q31f).
1845:- Statement: Per COMPOSITION ackOwnership (RULINGS Q31e, replacing Q28's ACK clause): the source of truth sends every ACK after its own publication (CO-ACK-AFTER-SOURCE-PUBLICATION, OBS-ACK-ORDER); the pull at the returned position is served by an index eligible for it, else by the fallback, so read-your-own-write is exact (CO-RYOW-ROUTED); during a current-index outage commits and ACKs continue and pulls fall back (CO-OUTAGE-ACKS-CONTINUE), and the index catches up from the feed through a bounded queue (CO-CATCHUP-BOUNDED-QUEUE).
1958:- Statement: Per COMPOSITION eligibility (RULINGS Q31d): an index serves basis B only when its watermark, a fully resolved prefix, has reached B in B's epoch (CO-EPOCH-MISMATCH), C1's conditions hold, it can reconstruct B (a current-only index only inside the validity interval of every attribute read, CO-RECONSTRUCT-OUTSIDE-VALIDITY) and it has applied every published erasure (CO-ERASURE-FRONTIER); a read with no eligible index waits at most T-WATERMARK-WAIT-MS (CO-WATERMARK-WAIT) and then routes to an eligible fallback (CO-WATERMARK-FALLBACK) whose latency counts in the read's own latency (CO-FALLBACK-LATENCY-COUNTS); the receipt records the route and the surface language, a cross-language fallback is counted per surface (CO-FALLBACK-LANGUAGE), and fallbacks are reported as a share of reads per window (CO-FALLBACK-SHARE, OBS-WATERMARK); no index answers for a basis it is not eligible for (CO-NO-STALE-ANSWER); history and analytics trail asynchronously behind their watermarks (CO-ASYNC-HISTORY).
2088:**`G9.erasure.protected-copies`: Erasure reaches every protected copy.**
2109:**`G9.erasure.reproduction-modulo`: Every reproduction contract holds modulo erasure.**
2316:- Cases: CS-EVAL-COUNTER (all, COMPILED); CS-EVAL-COUNTER (CX-CALIBRATION-EMPTY, CX-CALIBRATION-MISSING, CX-NS-MISSING-BAR, CX-NS-FEWER-RUNS, CX-NS-ECHOED-BASIS, CX-NS-UNFROZEN-TRACE, CX-GS-WRONG-SCENARIO, CX-GS-NO-WITNESSES, CX-SELECTION-SHORT, CX-ZERO-MODES, CX-COUNTEREXAMPLE-EDITED, CX-MUTANT-NO-REACH, CX-MUTANT-CRASH-KILL, CX-OBS-COVERAGE-GAP, CX-FAULT-REPS-SHORT, CX-STATIC-EXTRA, CX-SCALE-COUNT, CX-METRIC-MISSING, CX-REQ-NO-STATEMENT, CX-MATRIX-NO-EXCEPTION, CX-PROVENANCE-INPUT, CX-WITNESS-CLIENT-COUNTERS, CX-BUDGET-UNFROZEN, CX-SCREENING, CX-STALE-DEFINITION, CX-COMPOSITION-UNBOUND, CX-NO-VERIFIER, CX-W0-UNPINNED, CX-W0-FLOOR-MISSED, CX-P2-REJECTS-VALID, CX-POSITION-GATE, PX-PASS-ALL, PX-COUNTEREXAMPLE, PX-MUTANT-KILL, PX-OBSERVE, PX-FAULT, PX-STATIC, PX-SCALE, PX-METRICS, PX-NS, PX-GS, PX-REQUIREMENT, PX-CALIBRATION, PX-MATRIX, PX-PROVENANCE, PX-WITNESS, PX-BUDGET, PX-W0-COVERAGE, COMPILED).
