lab/acceptance/ACCEPTANCE.md:276:Every lane accepts at least [-(2^53-1), 2^53-1]. Every attribute used in a range rule (for example 'pay rate at or above 16.50', 'hours over 40') has an order-preserving comparison on every surface that serves the rule: native exact types inside their exact range, or a documented order-preserving channel.
lab/acceptance/ACCEPTANCE.md:278:**Decimal (RULINGS Q18).** declaration: every decimal attribute declares precision p (total significant digits) and scale s (fractional digits), 0 <= s <= p. storage: p <= 15 -> scaled integer value * 10^s (|scaled| < 10^15 < 2^53); p > 15 -> order-preserving decimal string (fixed-width, sign-aware encoding whose bytewise order equals numeric order). reject: a value with more than s fractional digits, or with more than p - s integer digits, fails the write with E-DECIMAL-UNREPRESENTABLE and leaves no residue; never rounded or truncated. family: decimal is its own family, ordered between number and datetime (CARD_MANY_ORDER); 1.50 and 1.5 are one value. comparison: CMP-DECIMAL-CROSS: comparison with integer or number is preflight E-MIXED-FAMILY unless the query converts explicitly. arithmetic: TypeScript kernel, exact decimal arithmetic; engine-side decimal arithmetic only where a projection needs it (RULINGS Q19). inputCapture: the writer captures the caller's original typed input before any normalization; tests assert nothing was rounded before capture (DEC-INPUT-CAPTURE, M-DECIMAL-PRECAPTURE-ROUND). kernelMaxDigits: 38.
lab/acceptance/ACCEPTANCE.md:289:| DO-CMP | = != < <= > >= between decimals | - | - | none; compares exact numeric value (1.50 = 1.5) | DEC-OP-COMPARE |
lab/acceptance/ACCEPTANCE.md:306:**Decimal test classes (RULINGS Q22).** DEC-ADJACENT-LARGE: adjacent 38-digit decimals (differing in the last digit) stay distinct and ordered on every surface; DEC-NEGATIVE: negative values, including order across zero; DEC-ZERO: 0, 0.00 and -0.00 are one value; DEC-SCALE-BOUNDARY: values with exactly s fractional digits and exactly p - s integer digits accepted; one more rejected; DEC-INTERMEDIATE: arithmetic intermediates are exact (no rounding before the final result); DEC-EVERY-PATH: every query and serialization path (Triples, repository, native, raw hatch, feed, journal, backup and restore) round-trips exactly; DEC-ORDER-KEY-INDEPENDENT: an independent checker compares the order-key byte order with exact numeric order over the whole CS-DECIMAL corpus; DEC-INPUT-CAPTURE: the writer's captured input equals the caller's original typed input before normalization.
lab/acceptance/ACCEPTANCE.md:325:| RS-RETIREMENT-CONTENT | snapshot retirement metadata is compared as the logical content {identity, value, recordedAt, knownRetirement: null or {retractedAt, retractTxId}}; native rows add retractedPosition; physical field names are EXP-R01's and the oracle renames them | RULINGS Q21 AMB-02 |
lab/acceptance/ACCEPTANCE.md:331:| JN-FIELDS | journal changes are compared on the documented fields plus the testkit-pinned ones (assert: value, validFrom, assertionTxId; retract: value, recordedAt, retractedAt, retractionTxId); byte identity of the whole journal is a separate T0-capture baseline | RULINGS Q21 AMB-05 |
