lab/acceptance/ACCEPTANCE.md:617:- A receipt made on a screening profile (SCREENING_PROFILES, RULINGS Q16) is evidence for candidate comparison only: it never passes VA, never closes an obligation, never feeds calibration and never carries forward.
lab/acceptance/ACCEPTANCE.md:632:A mutant counts only when (1) its reach probe fired at least once during a targeted case, and (2) at least one targeted case failed through a comparator mismatch on an identified assertion (case id and assertion id), not through an error, timeout, crash or setup failure. Mutants patch only the system under test; oracle, case and gate hashes are identical to the clean receipt.
lab/acceptance/ACCEPTANCE.md:736:- **Outcomes.** The oracle derives each command's expected outcome from intent, order, preconditions, enforcement (CN-NEW-OR-WORSENED) and durable-decision evidence (COMMIT_OUTCOMES), then compares the receipts' outcomes afterwards. A receipt never decides which command is valid or committed.
lab/acceptance/ACCEPTANCE.md:737:- **Outputs.** Complete assertion metadata; raw-lifetime and as-of snapshot history; entity models (card-one value or E-CONFLICTING-VALUES per C5; card-many per CARD_MANY_ORDER; absent optional as a missing property; includes at the same basis; timelines); transaction records with ordered changes and the logical journal facts (C6); cursor page sequences; support counts; C1 eligibility routes (for O-PLAN); arithmetic, comparison and aggregate results per section 4; analytic scale counts per population stratum (SCALE_POPULATION, section S).
lab/acceptance/ACCEPTANCE.md:743:Each case file entry carries: resultSemantics: set | bag | ordered; groupingKey: list of variables with COMPARISON_RULES identity; unboundHandling: exclude-row | null-cell (stated per projected variable); comparator: CMP-SET-ROWS | CMP-BAG-ROWS | CMP-ORDERED-ROWS; expectedRows; citation (SPARQL 1.1 or SQL section, or the packet task).
lab/acceptance/ACCEPTANCE.md:745:- Packet-derived shapes use set semantics (runner sorted-unique comparison).
lab/acceptance/ACCEPTANCE.md:746:- Negation controls compare the projected entity set.
lab/acceptance/ACCEPTANCE.md:747:- Aggregate controls follow AGGREGATE_RULES; empty groups per AG-EMPTY-*.
