lab/acceptance/ACCEPTANCE.md:1309:- Statement: Every CS-DECIMAL case, per DECIMAL_RULES (RULINGS Q18) and the operation, conversion and scale tables DECIMAL_OPS, DECIMAL_CONVERSIONS and DECIMAL_SCALE_EVOLUTION (RULINGS Q22), one named case per row, plus DECIMAL_TESTS (adjacent large decimals, negatives, zero, scale boundaries, arithmetic intermediates, every query and serialization path, an independent order-key check, and input capture before normalization): each decimal attribute declares precision and scale; precision <= 15 is stored as a scaled integer (DEC-P15-SCALED), larger precision as an order-preserving decimal string (DEC-P16-STRING); both round-trip exactly on every surface; every comparison with integer or number, equality included, is preflight E-MIXED-FAMILY (DEC-CROSS-FAMILY-PREFLIGHT) and exact after explicit conversion (DEC-CONVERTED-COMPARE); results beyond the precision fail with E-DECIMAL-OVERFLOW, bare / with E-DECIMAL-BARE-DIVIDE, decimal to integer with a fraction with E-DECIMAL-FRACTION, and a narrowing migration that would lose digits with E-DECIMAL-NARROWING, atomically; range rules (for example 'pay rate at or above 16.50') compare in exact numeric order on the repository, fragments and documented raw channel; a value with more fractional digits than the scale (DEC-SCALE-EXCESS) or outside the precision (DEC-PRECISION-EXCESS) fails with E-DECIMAL-UNREPRESENTABLE, never rounded; kernel arithmetic over decimals is exact.
lab/acceptance/ACCEPTANCE.md:1423:**`REQ.no-silent-precision-loss`: Requirement: No silent precision loss: exact storage and round trip for every value kind in use, order-preserving comparison for range-rule attributes, a hard error never silent conversion, integer range of at least 2^53, arithmetic over many rows only where a projection needs it.**
lab/acceptance/ACCEPTANCE.md:1424:- Statement: No silent precision loss: exact storage and round trip for every value kind in use, order-preserving comparison for range-rule attributes, a hard error never silent conversion, integer range of at least 2^53, arithmetic over many rows only where a projection needs it. Each engine declares a route for this requirement, NATIVE or WORKAROUND (with its design id and a plain statement of what the engine cannot do natively); the requirement's own CS-REQ tests pass on that route. An open requirement never removes an engine from comparison. Starting points: XTDB: BIGINT, DECIMAL and VARCHAR store exactly; kernel arithmetic; split-sum only where a projection sums; QLever: lexical channels and fixed-width hex order keys; 60-bit integers cover 2^53; reject beyond +/-2^59 at write; kernel arithmetic.
lab/acceptance/ACCEPTANCE.md:1464:**`G2.expr.cross-family-comparison`: Comparisons follow the frozen comparison table.**
lab/acceptance/ACCEPTANCE.md:1587:- Statement: Every C5-* case of CS-CONFLICT: Equal-valued duplicates are not conflicts (one value, several supports); a conflict is two or more distinct live values of a cardinality-one attribute at the basis; get and getMany fail with E-CONFLICTING-VALUES listing every conflicted entity and attribute (compared on _tag, reason and the set of {entityId, attribute}, AMB-13); counts, ordering, includes and negation fail with it when a referenced attribute is conflicted for any candidate; find also fails with it when a returned document contains a conflicted attribute even if the filter avoids it, while a projection that omits the attribute succeeds (RS-FIND-CONFLICT, RULINGS Q21 AMB-17, provisional, flagged for Sam); reads that neither reference nor return a conflicted attribute are unaffected; the values(attribute) relation lists every live value with its supports; the raw convenience shape returns its documented indicator and never certifies equivalence.
lab/acceptance/ACCEPTANCE.md:1698:- Statement: Long sweeps pin a log position, not a long database transaction. Each engine declares a route for this requirement, NATIVE or WORKAROUND (with its design id and a plain statement of what the engine cannot do natively); the requirement's own CS-REQ tests pass on that route. An open requirement never removes an engine from comparison. Starting points: XTDB: snapshot token or system-time basis; QLever: position in the log; one request per page.
lab/acceptance/ACCEPTANCE.md:1808:- Statement: Per-subject atomic, idempotent commit with lost-ACK resolution. Each engine declares a route for this requirement, NATIVE or WORKAROUND (with its design id and a plain statement of what the engine cannot do natively); the requirement's own CS-REQ tests pass on that route. An open requirement never removes an engine from comparison. Starting points: XTDB: native transactions, ASSERT for CAS, claims table; QLever: log of record plus broker (PLAN C2, C3).
