   172	2. **Select by priority order:** the highest-priority unmet objective (P1 first, then P2, and so on) with a feasible experiment goes first (corrected after the Codex plan-v2 review, finding 12); correctness
   173	   obligations it depends on are pulled forward. Keep two or three rival hypotheses per bottleneck; at most two unintegrated
   174	   branches per lane; an obligation with no progress for two generations escalates.
   175	3. **Brief and dispatch** with the template in 6.3.
   176	4. **Build and run** in the agent's own worktree on `exp/<id>-<slug>`, gates through `lab/bin`.
   177	5. **Verify** on the integrated candidate by an agent that did not write it.
   178	6. **Promote** only when correctness invariants hold and the north-star measurements and golden scenarios improve or hold against
   179	   frozen controls, with cumulative cost inside the frozen budgets.
   180	7. **Next generation:** mutate winners, retire hypotheses that failed twice for the same reason. A failed falsifier blocks its
   181	   dependents.
