   613	### 5.7 Applicability, carry-forward and fresh final acceptance
   614	
   615	- Bound identities: imported source files; imported dist files; engine image digest; engine configuration; resource caps; fixture contents; enabled capabilities; gate script versions; oracle file versions; case manifests; acceptance-rule version (contract transitive hash and obligation definition hash).
   616	- A receipt carries forward to a later profile only when every bound identity is unchanged, checked by an explicit applicability record (AP) that recomputes each identity on the later profile. Carry-forward serves intermediate tracking only.
   617	- A receipt made on a screening profile (SCREENING_PROFILES, RULINGS Q16) is evidence for candidate comparison only: it never passes VA, never closes an obligation, never feeds calibration and never carries forward.
   618	
   619	- The final acceptance of the selected integrated profile is entirely fresh: every obligation, including scale rungs and load levels, runs on that profile; nothing carries into it.
   620	
   621	### 5.8 Verifier coverage
   622	
   623	| Mode | Rule |
   624	| --- | --- |
   625	| rerun | The verifier reruns the obligation's full selection on the same profile and recomputes every verdict from retained objects. |
   626	| re-evaluate-and-spot | The verifier independently re-evaluates every retained answer byte, fault outcome and coverage record for every ladder level, scenario, rung and run, and performs at least one spot rerun per profile unit (one per lane and NS measurement; one per lane and golden scenario; one per lane and rung). |
   627	
   628	Every obligation's verifier mode is listed with it in section 10.
   629	
   630	### 5.9 Mutation controls
   631	
   632	A mutant counts only when (1) its reach probe fired at least once during a targeted case, and (2) at least one targeted case failed through a comparator mismatch on an identified assertion (case id and assertion id), not through an error, timeout, crash or setup failure. Mutants patch only the system under test; oracle, case and gate hashes are identical to the clean receipt.
   633	
   634	| Mutant | Fault | Reach probe | Targets |
   635	| --- | --- | --- | --- |
   636	| M-HALF-OPEN | validTo treated as inclusive (or validFrom as exclusive) in the visibility filter | visibility.validInterval | CS-TEMPORAL:boundary, CS-ENTITY:valid-boundary |
   637	| M-DROPPED-SUPPORT | retracting one of two supports removes the value or derived fact | support.retract | CS-SUPPORT:duplicate-support, CS-SUPPORT-DAG:partial-retraction, CS-CONFLICT:C5-EQ-DUP |
   638	| M-FUTURE-RETIREMENT | snapshot reads return retirements recorded after the cut | history.snapshotMask | CS-HAM9:snapshot, CS-CFG8:retirement-metadata-target |
   639	| M-INTEGER-ROUND | integers pass through binary64 | codec.integer | CS-TYPES8:integer-edges, CS-NUMERIC:integer-scalar |
   640	| M-OUT-OF-RANGE-WRAP | an integer outside the lane's range is stored wrapped or rounded instead of rejected | write.integerRange | CS-RANGE-OUT:all |
   641	| M-DECIMAL-ROUND | a decimal beyond its declared scale is rounded instead of rejected | codec.decimal | CS-DECIMAL:unrepresentable |
   642	| M-DECIMAL-PRECAPTURE-ROUND | the writer normalizes (rounds) a decimal before capturing the caller's typed input | write.captureInput | CS-DECIMAL:DEC-INPUT-CAPTURE |
   643	| M-ERASURE-LEAK | an erased value stays readable from one inventoried location or derived channel (order key, lexical channel, restored backup) | erasure.apply | CS-ERASURE:ER-ORDER-KEY-CHANNEL, CS-ERASURE:ER-RESTORE-PRE-BACKUP |
   644	| M-STALE-INDEX-ANSWER | an index answers for a basis beyond its watermark, or a current-only index answers for a basis it cannot reconstruct | route.watermark | CS-COMPOSITION:CO-NO-STALE-ANSWER, CS-COMPOSITION:CO-RECONSTRUCT-OUTSIDE-VALIDITY |
   645	| M-ACK-BEFORE-PUBLICATION | the source sends the ACK before its own publication | commit.ack | CS-COMPOSITION:CO-ACK-AFTER-SOURCE-PUBLICATION |
   646	| M-RYOW-STALE-ROUTE | the pull at the returned position is served by an index that is not yet eligible for it | route.ryow | CS-COMPOSITION:CO-RYOW-ROUTED, CS-COMPOSITION:CO-OUTAGE-ACKS-CONTINUE |
